  {
   "t": 23.14,
   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "Replay of 1 Sep 2021 Ida rain over Queens, study area `nyc-queens-v0`:\n\nStorm used for both runs:\n\n* **118 mm in 4 h, center_peaked, rain over the whole study area** - the `Ida 1 Sep 2021 (LaGuardia gauge)` case\n* `sim_hours: 8` to allow ponded water to drain\n* Planning model, not a forecast.\n\n### Baseline - no change to sewers\n\nRun `r_e5558564426152f5`:\n\n* 12,531 buildings flooded, of which 4,975 severe\n* 45,385 people exposed\n* 92.198 km road impassable at >0.3 m\n* 2.2384 km2 flooded\n* max depth 4.521 m in domain\n* drained 1,163,496.2 m3, stored at end 729,052.4 m3\n\nAll neighbourhoods checked flood:\n\n* **Elmhurst:** 3,012 buildings flooded, max_depth 2.9 m, 27.055 km road impassable, 10,775 people exposed, 0.6364 km2 flooded\n* **Jackson Heights:** 2,782 buildings flooded, max_depth 2.279 m, 15.922 km road impassable, 9,318 people exposed, 0.4241 km2 flooded\n* **Corona:** 2,006 buildings flooded, max_depth 4.52 m - deepest of those checked, domain max, 25.635 km road impassable, 14,063 people exposed - highest people count, 0.5411 km2 flooded\n* **Woodside:** 1,452 buildings flooded, max_depth 2.812 m, 9.529 km road impassable, 3,429 people exposed, 0.1881 km2 flooded\n* **Middle Village:** 1,359 buildings flooded, max_depth 1.479 m, 5.895 km road impassable, 1,061 people exposed, 0.1043 km2 flooded\n* **East Elmhurst:** 935 buildings flooded, max_depth 1.438 m, 6.893 km road impassable, 1,933 people exposed, 0.1526 km2 flooded\n\n> Rank by buildings flooded: Elmhurst > Jackson Heights > Corona > Woodside > Middle Village > East Elmhurst\n> Rank by depth: Corona 4.52m > Elmhurst 2.9m > Woodside 2.812m > Jackson Heights 2.279m > Middle Village 1.479m > East Elmhurst 1.438m\n> Rank by people: Corona > Elmhurst > Jackson Heights\n\n### Would doubling sewer capacity have helped?\n\nTested city-wide doubling of existing drains - `drain_upgrade capacity_factor: 2.0` with no place, so applied to WHOLE study area, same 118mm / 4h storm.\n\nRun `r_525e918dbc221462`:\n\n* 9,113 buildings flooded vs 12,531 baseline: -3,418, -27%\n* 1,963 buildings severe vs 4,975 baseline: -3,012, -61%\n* 21,324 people exposed vs 45,385: -24,061, -53%\n* 44.154 km road impassable vs 92.198 km: -48.044 km, -52%\n* 1.0691 km2 flooded vs 2.2384 km2: -52%\n* max depth 2.306 m vs 4.521 m\n* drained volume 1,859,186.1 m3 vs 1,163,496.2 m3, stored at end 206,063.3 m3 vs 729,052.4 m3\n\nYes - doubling existing sewer capacity substantially reduces severe flooding, people exposed and impassable roads by about half, and severe buildings by ~60%.\n\nIt does not prevent flooding: >9,000 buildings still flood and >44 km of road remains impassable in this replay."
   }
